WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.535 --> 00:00:06.529
♪ ♪

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:06.801
♪ ♪

00:00:06.835 --> 00:00:08.567
&gt;&gt; Bret: THIS WEEK MILLIONS OF

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:09.278
AMERICANS EXPERIENCED A

00:00:09.279 --> 00:00:11.135
THANKSGIVING LIKE NO OTHER WITH

00:00:11.136 --> 00:00:12.627
HEIGHTENED RESTRICTIONS PUT IN

00:00:12.661 --> 00:00:14.018
PLACE BY GOVERNORS ACROSS THE

00:00:14.053 --> 00:00:16.666
COUNTRY AND RESPONSE TO SPIKES

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:17.475
IN CORONAVIRUS CASES.

00:00:17.476 --> 00:00:19.771
JOINING ME NOW FROM LITTLE ROCK

00:00:19.772 --> 00:00:20.813
IS ARKANSAS

00:00:20.847 --> 00:00:22.583
GOVERNOR ASA HUTCHINSON, VICE

00:00:22.585 --> 00:00:23.953
CHAIR OF THE NATIONAL GOVERNORS

00:00:23.955 --> 00:00:24.662
ASSOCIATION.

00:00:24.697 --> 00:00:25.805
GOVERNOR, WELCOME TO

00:00:25.806 --> 00:00:26.731
"FOX NEWS SUNDAY"."

00:00:26.732 --> 00:00:27.250
&gt;&gt; Governor Hutchinson:

00:00:27.284 --> 00:00:29.490
THANK YOU, BRET, IT IS GOOD TO

00:00:29.524 --> 00:00:30.307
BE WITH YOU TODAY.

00:00:30.308 --> 00:00:33.116
&gt;&gt; Bret: ARKANSAS HAS BEEN

00:00:33.117 --> 00:00:35.297
DEALING WITH THIS, AND WHERE DO

00:00:35.299 --> 00:00:37.931
YOU THINK YOUR STATE IS JUST AND

00:00:37.932 --> 00:00:39.090
HOSPITALIZATIONS AS OF LAST WEEK

00:00:39.091 --> 00:00:39.611
FRIDAY?

00:00:39.612 --> 00:00:42.160
IT SURPASSED 1,000 FOR THE FIRST

00:00:42.161 --> 00:00:43.117
TIME IN YOUR STATE.

00:00:43.119 --> 00:00:45.782
A TOUGH NUMBER.

00:00:45.783 --> 00:00:46.927
WHERE ARE YOU?

00:00:46.928 --> 00:00:49.392
&gt;&gt; WELL, THE HOSPITALIZATIONS IS

00:00:49.393 --> 00:00:51.844
THE GREAT CONCERN AND THAT IS A

00:00:51.845 --> 00:00:54.805
RECORD NUMBER OF COVID PATIENTS

00:00:54.806 --> 00:00:57.074
THAT WE THOUGHT HOSPITALIZED.

00:00:57.108 --> 00:00:58.170
IT HOPEFULLY WILL STABILIZE.

00:00:58.205 --> 00:01:00.887
WE HAVE A HOSPITAL GROUP THAT’S

00:01:00.888 --> 00:01:02.894
WORKING WITH ME VERY CLOSELY TO

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:06.570
MAKE SURE THAT WE CONTINUE TO

00:01:06.571 --> 00:01:08.347
HAVE ADEQUATE HOSPITAL SPACE FOR

00:01:08.349 --> 00:01:09.382
BOTH COVID PATIENTS, WHICH IS

00:01:09.384 --> 00:01:11.187
REALLY A MINORITY OF THOSE THAT

00:01:11.188 --> 00:01:13.207
ARE IN THE HOSPITAL, AS WELL AS

00:01:13.242 --> 00:01:15.543
CARING FOR ALL THE OTHER

00:01:15.544 --> 00:01:17.379
HEALTH CARE NEEDS THAT WE HAVE.

00:01:17.381 --> 00:01:19.401
DURING THE LAST THREE WEEKS

00:01:19.436 --> 00:01:21.398
SINCE WE’VE HAD THIS MOST RECENT

00:01:21.399 --> 00:01:22.997
SPIKE, THE PEOPLE OF ARKANSAS

00:01:23.032 --> 00:01:23.904
ARE TAKING THIS EXTRAORDINARILY

00:01:23.939 --> 00:01:24.734
SERIOUSLY.

00:01:24.735 --> 00:01:27.740
I THINK WE HAD A VERY SUBDUED

00:01:27.741 --> 00:01:27.958
THANKSGIVING.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.160
WE ARE VERY THANKFUL, BUT AT THE

00:01:30.194 --> 00:01:32.348
SAME TIME, PEOPLE UNDERSTAND THE

00:01:32.349 --> 00:01:35.409
RISK OF LARGE GATHERINGS AND THE

00:01:35.444 --> 00:01:37.036
IMPORTANCE OF SOCIAL DISTANCING.

00:01:37.038 --> 00:01:39.168
WE ARE TRYING TO TAKE THE

00:01:39.169 --> 00:01:41.983
APPROACH THAT WE WANT TO MAKE

00:01:42.018 --> 00:01:43.396
SURE THAT OUR GUIDELINES ARE

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:44.022
FOLLOWED.

00:01:44.056 --> 00:01:45.460
WE’VE INCREASED OUR ENFORCEMENT

00:01:45.494 --> 00:01:46.174
EFFORTS.

00:01:46.175 --> 00:01:48.280
WE’VE WORKED WITH OUR HOSPITALS

00:01:48.314 --> 00:01:50.581
TO MAKE SURE THAT WE HAVE SPACE

00:01:50.615 --> 00:01:51.021
THERE.

00:01:51.022 --> 00:01:53.128
WE ARE NOT TRYING TO SHUT DOWN

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:54.673
BUSINESSES THAT ARE DOING A

00:01:54.674 --> 00:01:55.211
GOOD JOB.

00:01:55.212 --> 00:01:56.771
WE STILL HAVE SOME LIMITATIONS

00:01:56.772 --> 00:01:59.034
AND SPACING IN OUR RESTAURANTS

00:01:59.035 --> 00:02:00.110
AND GYMS.

00:02:00.111 --> 00:02:02.285
THOSE ARE IMPORTANT TO BE

00:02:02.287 --> 00:02:03.940
ENFORCED BUT WE REALIZE THAT YOU

00:02:03.941 --> 00:02:05.571
COULD REALLY INCREASE PROBLEMS

00:02:05.572 --> 00:02:09.005
ACROSS THE BOARD IF YOU START

00:02:09.007 --> 00:02:09.968
SHUTTING DOWN BUSINESSES,

00:02:10.003 --> 00:02:11.967
PUTTING PEOPLE UNEMPLOYED AS WE

00:02:12.002 --> 00:02:14.192
GO INTO THE CHRISTMAS SEASON.

00:02:14.194 --> 00:02:15.200
&gt;&gt; Bret: YOU MENTIONED

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:16.203
ENFORCEMENT, YOU HAVE A

00:02:16.204 --> 00:02:16.930
STATEWIDE MASK MANDATE AND

00:02:16.964 --> 00:02:18.082
YOU’VE HAD SOME DOCTORS WRITE

00:02:18.116 --> 00:02:19.699
YOU A LETTER SAYING THEY WOULD

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:21.039
REALLY LIKE YOU TO ENFORCE THAT.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.668
IT STATES THAT IT COULD RESULT

00:02:22.669 --> 00:02:23.704
IN A $500 FINE.

00:02:23.706 --> 00:02:28.148
ARE YOU DOING THAT ON A MASK

00:02:28.183 --> 00:02:29.083
MANDATE FRONT?

00:02:29.117 --> 00:02:30.113
&gt;&gt; Governor Hutchinson: WELL,

00:02:30.147 --> 00:02:32.602
IN TERMS OF OUR RESTAURANTS, OUR

00:02:32.604 --> 00:02:33.615
REGULATED INDUSTRIES, WE HAVE

00:02:33.616 --> 00:02:35.085
INSPECTIONS, WE ARE ENFORCING

00:02:35.119 --> 00:02:37.886
THE MASK MANDATE, THE SPACING

00:02:37.887 --> 00:02:39.527
REQUIREMENTS AS WELL.

00:02:39.562 --> 00:02:41.216
IN TERMS OF THE GENERAL

00:02:41.251 --> 00:02:43.322
POPULATION, WE HAVE TO RELY UPON

00:02:43.356 --> 00:02:46.697
OUR LOCAL LAW ENFORCEMENT AND

00:02:46.698 --> 00:02:48.513
THAT’S A GAP, BECAUSE THERE’S A

00:02:48.547 --> 00:02:50.296
LOT OF HESITANCY ABOUT GOING OUT

00:02:50.297 --> 00:02:52.852
AND ARRESTING SOMEONE FOR NOT

00:02:52.854 --> 00:02:55.927
HAVING A MASK ON, AND SO THERE’S

00:02:55.929 --> 00:02:57.823
A WARNING THAT’S GIVEN, WE ARE

00:02:57.857 --> 00:02:59.707
WORKING WITH OUR OFFICIALS TO

00:02:59.741 --> 00:03:01.651
INCREASE THAT EDUCATION PART OF

00:03:01.685 --> 00:03:03.880
IT AND THE COMPLIANCE EFFORTS ON

00:03:03.915 --> 00:03:04.443
THE MASK.

00:03:04.477 --> 00:03:05.928
EVERYBODY KNOWS WHAT NEEDS TO BE

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:08.500
DONE AND WE HAVE THAT MASK

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:10.595
MANDATE IN ARKANSAS, VAST

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:11.718
MAJORITY ARE FOLLOWING THAT.

00:03:11.719 --> 00:03:13.655
WE PUT IN MILLIONS OF DOLLARS

00:03:13.656 --> 00:03:16.016
INTO AN AD CAMPAIGN STRESSING

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.137
THE SCIENCE BEHIND THE REASON WE

00:03:18.138 --> 00:03:19.305
NEED TO DO THAT.

00:03:19.306 --> 00:03:20.748
I THINK THAT’S THE RIGHT

00:03:20.749 --> 00:03:21.750
APPROACH, WE ARE ALWAYS LOOKING

00:03:21.784 --> 00:03:23.907
FOR MORE WAYS TO STRENGTHEN THAT

00:03:23.941 --> 00:03:25.293
COMPLIANCE AND MAKE IT BETTER.

00:03:25.295 --> 00:03:26.798
&gt;&gt; Bret: ON THE FLIP SIDE, YOU

00:03:26.799 --> 00:03:28.429
HAVE MADE CLEAR, AND YOU JUST

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:31.367
DID, THAT THERE WILL BE NO

00:03:31.368 --> 00:03:32.499
SHUTDOWN OF BUSINESSES AGAIN.

00:03:32.533 --> 00:03:33.557
&gt;&gt; Governor Hutchinson: WELL,

00:03:33.558 --> 00:03:34.742
I DON’T KNOW IF YOU EVER SAY

00:03:34.777 --> 00:03:37.105
NEVER, BUT THAT’S THE LAST THING

00:03:37.139 --> 00:03:38.717
THAT WE WANT TO DO AND

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:39.614
PARTICULARLY SHUTTING DOWN A

00:03:39.616 --> 00:03:41.274
BUSINESS THAT HAS WORKED HARD

00:03:41.309 --> 00:03:43.428
FOR THE LAST EIGHT MONTHS TO

00:03:43.463 --> 00:03:46.358
COMPLY WITH EVERY PUBLIC HEALTH

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:48.843
DIRECTIVE AND THEY HAVE A SAFE

00:03:48.844 --> 00:03:50.274
POSITIONS WITHIN THEIR

00:03:50.275 --> 00:03:51.736
RESTAURANT AND THEY HAVE NO

00:03:51.737 --> 00:03:53.344
CASES COMING OUT OF IT.

00:03:53.345 --> 00:03:54.705
AND SO THAT TO ME IS JUST

00:03:54.739 --> 00:03:56.858
FUNDAMENTALLY WRONG TO SAY

00:03:56.893 --> 00:03:58.528
YOU’RE OUT OF BUSINESS NOW AND

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.426
THAT YOUR WORKERS ARE

00:04:00.461 --> 00:04:01.293
UNEMPLOYED, PARTICULARLY

00:04:01.328 --> 00:04:03.817
WHENEVER THERE’S NOT ANY CARES

00:04:03.818 --> 00:04:05.292
ACT RELIEF PACKAGE ANYMORE.

00:04:05.294 --> 00:04:07.233
THAT MONEY HAS BEEN ALLOCATED.

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:08.556
WE’VE TRIED TO HELP OUR SMALL

00:04:08.557 --> 00:04:10.530
BUSINESSES, BUT WE ARE NOT ABLE

00:04:10.565 --> 00:04:13.023
TO COMPENSATE SOMEONE FOR THEIR

00:04:13.024 --> 00:04:15.643
LOSS OF A JOB, FOR THEIR LOSS OF

00:04:15.644 --> 00:04:16.888
AN INCOME AND SHUTTING DOWN THE

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:17.216
BUSINESS.

00:04:17.217 --> 00:04:19.691
SO WE WANT TO BE SMART ABOUT IT

00:04:19.693 --> 00:04:22.084
AND SO WE DID PUT AN 11:00 P.M.

00:04:22.085 --> 00:04:23.656
CURFEW ON BARS AND RESTAURANTS

00:04:23.658 --> 00:04:24.980
TRYING TO BREAK UP THE LATE

00:04:24.981 --> 00:04:26.261
NIGHT CROWDS.

00:04:26.262 --> 00:04:29.094
BUT AT THE SAME TIME, WE DON’T

00:04:29.095 --> 00:04:30.180
WANT TO OVERLY RESTRICT OUR

00:04:30.214 --> 00:04:31.823
BUSINESSES THAT ARE DOING A

00:04:31.857 --> 00:04:34.506
GOOD JOB OUT THERE, BECAUSE THAT

00:04:34.508 --> 00:04:35.724
JUST MAKE THE PROBLEM WORSE.

00:04:35.726 --> 00:04:37.030
&gt;&gt; Bret: SHOULD ARKANSAS

00:04:37.031 --> 00:04:39.043
STUDENTS BE BACK IN SCHOOL

00:04:39.044 --> 00:04:40.912
PHYSICALLY AS OPPOSED TO

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:41.225
VIRTUALLY?

00:04:41.226 --> 00:04:43.139
&gt;&gt; Governor Hutchinson: I’LL

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.891
TELL YOU A STORY, I JUST KNOW OF

00:04:45.925 --> 00:04:48.324
A COUPLE THAT ARE BOTH WORKING

00:04:48.326 --> 00:04:49.948
IN THE SCHOOL HAD TO GO VIRTUAL

00:04:49.949 --> 00:04:51.874
AND SO WHAT YOU DO WITH THE

00:04:51.875 --> 00:04:53.196
CHILDREN WHEN BOTH PARENTS ARE

00:04:53.198 --> 00:04:53.519
WORKING?

00:04:53.553 --> 00:04:56.259
THEY HAD THEM STAY OVER AT A

00:04:56.293 --> 00:04:58.440
FRIEND’S HOUSE AND THE CHILD WAS

00:04:58.441 --> 00:05:00.882
POSITIVE WITHIN DAYS BECAUSE OF

00:05:00.883 --> 00:05:01.905
THE FRIEND.

00:05:01.906 --> 00:05:04.151
AND SO THE IMPORTANT THING IS

00:05:04.152 --> 00:05:06.112
THAT THE SCHOOL IS A SAFE

00:05:06.113 --> 00:05:06.585
ENVIRONMENT.

00:05:06.587 --> 00:05:08.680
WE HAVE THE OPTION TO GO VIRTUAL

00:05:08.682 --> 00:05:10.775
AND TO PIVOT THERE BASED UPON

00:05:10.776 --> 00:05:12.412
LOCAL DECISIONS AND LOCAL CASES,

00:05:12.447 --> 00:05:14.236
BUT TO SAY CARTE BLANCHE WE ARE

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:16.343
GOING TO CLOSE OUR SCHOOLS, WE

00:05:16.345 --> 00:05:17.767
ARE NOT GOING TO HAVE THE IN

00:05:17.801 --> 00:05:19.782
CLASSROOM STRUCTURE AS AN OPTION

00:05:19.784 --> 00:05:22.100
WOULD REALLY HAVE SOME ADVERSE

00:05:22.134 --> 00:05:23.652
CONSEQUENCES THAT WE DON’T NEED

00:05:23.654 --> 00:05:24.673
AND ARE NOT NECESSARY.

00:05:24.675 --> 00:05:26.994
AND SO WE WANT TO BE ABLE TO

00:05:26.995 --> 00:05:29.576
KEEP THOSE OPEN WITH THE OPTION

00:05:29.577 --> 00:05:31.570
TO PIVOT TO VIRTUAL BASED UPON

00:05:31.572 --> 00:05:33.078
LOCAL CIRCUMSTANCES BUT WE WANT

00:05:33.113 --> 00:05:34.579
TO MINIMIZE THAT EFFORT WHEN WE

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:35.005
CAN.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:36.554
GOING TO SCHOOL IS VERY

00:05:36.556 --> 00:05:36.989
IMPORTANT.

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:39.043
ON THE HIGHER EDUCATION SIDE,

00:05:39.044 --> 00:05:40.744
YOU KNOW, AS OUR STUDENTS COME

00:05:40.778 --> 00:05:41.852
BACK, WE WANT THEM TO GET

00:05:41.887 --> 00:05:42.355
TESTED.

00:05:42.389 --> 00:05:44.038
WE WANT THEM TO -- IF THEY’VE

00:05:44.073 --> 00:05:46.463
BEEN IN A HOT ZONE OR THEY’VE

00:05:46.464 --> 00:05:48.278
BEEN AMONG PEOPLE OR NOT

00:05:48.279 --> 00:05:49.345
PROTECTED, TO MAKE SURE THEY

00:05:49.346 --> 00:05:51.566
ISOLATE OR THEY GET TESTED AS

00:05:51.567 --> 00:05:52.348
THEY COME BACK.

00:05:52.349 --> 00:05:55.043
&gt;&gt; Bret: I WANT TO TURN FOR A

00:05:55.077 --> 00:05:56.388
MINUTE TO THE ELECTION.

00:05:56.422 --> 00:05:57.896
PRESIDENT TRUMP, GOVERNOR, AS

00:05:57.931 --> 00:05:59.557
YOU KNOW HAS NOT CONCEDED THE

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:00.085
ELECTION.

00:06:00.119 --> 00:06:02.493
HE CONTINUES TO SAY THAT IT WAS

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:02.786
STOLEN.

00:06:02.787 --> 00:06:03.891
COMPUTER EXPERTS WITHIN HIS OWN

00:06:03.893 --> 00:06:04.479
ADMINISTRATION HAVE PUSHED BACK

00:06:04.514 --> 00:06:06.417
ON THAT.

00:06:06.451 --> 00:06:07.922
TAKE A LISTEN.

00:06:07.923 --> 00:06:09.731
&gt;&gt; THERE HAS BEEN SO MUCH FRAUD

00:06:09.733 --> 00:06:11.503
THAT WE HAVE UNCOVERED AS A

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:12.516
CAMPAIGN AND LISTEN, PEOPLE NEED

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:14.463
TO KNOW GOING FORWARD, IT’S NOT

00:06:14.497 --> 00:06:15.477
JUST ABOUT RIGHT NOW.

00:06:15.478 --> 00:06:17.268
WE NEED TO KNOW THAT EVERY

00:06:17.269 --> 00:06:18.860
ELECTION WE HOLD IN THE

00:06:18.862 --> 00:06:20.242
UNITED STATES OF AMERICA IS FAIR

00:06:20.243 --> 00:06:22.917
AND LEGAL AND EVERY LEGITIMATE

00:06:22.918 --> 00:06:23.986
BOAT GETS COUNTED.

00:06:23.987 --> 00:06:25.669
&gt;&gt; IT’S THE MOST SECURE IN

00:06:25.704 --> 00:06:26.184
AMERICAN HISTORY.

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:28.354
THERE IS NO EVIDENCE THAT ANY

00:06:28.356 --> 00:06:31.674
VOTING SYSTEM DELETED OR LOST

00:06:31.708 --> 00:06:34.390
VOTES OR CHANGED VOTES OR WAS IN

00:06:34.391 --> 00:06:35.413
ANY WAY COMPROMISED.

00:06:35.414 --> 00:06:37.694
&gt;&gt; I STAND BY THAT.

00:06:37.696 --> 00:06:40.201
THE AMERICAN PEOPLE SHOULD HAVE

00:06:40.235 --> 00:06:41.871
100% CONFIDENCE IN THEIR VOTE.

00:06:41.872 --> 00:06:44.415
&gt;&gt; Bret: SO GOVERNOR, HAVE YOU

00:06:44.417 --> 00:06:45.567
SEEN ANYTHING THAT SUGGESTS THAT

00:06:45.601 --> 00:06:47.513
THERE IS EVIDENCE THAT THE

00:06:47.514 --> 00:06:48.490
PRESIDENT COULD PREVAIL IN

00:06:48.491 --> 00:06:49.627
OVERTURNING THE ELECTION THAT

00:06:49.629 --> 00:06:51.743
HAS ALREADY BEEN CERTIFIED IN A

00:06:51.745 --> 00:06:53.437
NUMBER OF KEY STATES?

00:06:53.438 --> 00:06:54.759
&gt;&gt; Governor Hutchinson: MOST

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:57.023
IMPORTANTLY THE COURTS HAVE NOT

00:06:57.024 --> 00:06:58.267
SEEN ANY EVIDENCE OF SUCH

00:06:58.268 --> 00:07:00.132
EXTENSIVE FRAUD THAT THEY HAVE

00:07:00.166 --> 00:07:01.195
TO CHANGE THE RESULT.

00:07:01.196 --> 00:07:03.461
SCORES OF COURTS HAVE LOOKED AT

00:07:03.463 --> 00:07:06.850
THAT AND SO THAT’S WHY THE

00:07:06.851 --> 00:07:08.220
GENERAL SERVICE ADMINISTRATION

00:07:08.254 --> 00:07:10.685
RECOGNIZED VICE PRESIDENT BIDEN

00:07:10.719 --> 00:07:11.666
AS PRESIDENT-ELECT.

00:07:11.667 --> 00:07:13.002
HE IS PRESIDENT-ELECT.

00:07:13.037 --> 00:07:15.556
WE NEED TO WORK THAT TRANSITION.

00:07:15.558 --> 00:07:17.879
I APPLAUD PRESIDENT TRUMP FOR

00:07:17.881 --> 00:07:19.979
INITIATING THAT TRANSITION AND

00:07:20.013 --> 00:07:21.524
MAKING SURE THAT THAT IS

00:07:21.558 --> 00:07:21.792
HAPPENING.

00:07:21.793 --> 00:07:24.454
THE WORST THING THAT COULD

00:07:24.455 --> 00:07:26.528
HAPPEN IS THAT WE DO NOT HAVE A

00:07:26.562 --> 00:07:28.772
SMOOTH HANDOFF WHEN IT COMES TO

00:07:28.773 --> 00:07:31.640
OUR VACCINE DISTRIBUTION, PLANS,

00:07:31.674 --> 00:07:33.708
OUR WORK SPEED, AND THAT TAKES

00:07:33.709 --> 00:07:35.829
THAT TRANSITION TO START NOW AND

00:07:35.863 --> 00:07:36.977
I’M GRATEFUL THAT IT HAS.

00:07:37.011 --> 00:07:38.527
BUT I DO THINK WHEN YOU LOOK AT

00:07:38.528 --> 00:07:41.752
THE ELECTIONS, IT WOULD BE GOOD

00:07:41.754 --> 00:07:43.999
AFTER THE FACT THAT WE HAVE A

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.079
BIPARTISAN REVIEW AS TO WHAT’S

00:07:45.114 --> 00:07:46.964
BEST PRACTICES, BECAUSE THIS IS

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:48.698
GOING TO COME UP AGAIN AS TO HOW

00:07:48.732 --> 00:07:50.163
TO HANDLE ABSENTEE VOTES, WHAT’S

00:07:50.164 --> 00:07:52.461
THE BEST WAY TO PROTECT THE

00:07:52.496 --> 00:07:53.909
INTEGRITY OF THOSE VOTES TO GIVE

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.351
PEOPLE CONFIDENCE.

00:07:55.352 --> 00:07:57.820
AND THAT’S NOT TO SAY EVERYTHING

00:07:57.822 --> 00:07:58.838
WAS FRAUDULENT IN THIS ELECTION,

00:07:58.839 --> 00:08:01.228
IT JUST SAYS THAT WE NEED TO

00:08:01.229 --> 00:08:02.866
LEARN FROM EACH OTHER, ALL THE

00:08:02.867 --> 00:08:04.375
50 STATES, AND WHAT WE HAVE DONE

00:08:04.409 --> 00:08:07.385
AND HOW WE CAN DO IT BETTER AND

00:08:07.419 --> 00:08:09.987
TO GIVE PEOPLE CONFIDENCE THAT

00:08:09.988 --> 00:08:11.716
IS SO IMPORTANT IN OUR DEMOCRACY

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:11.919
DEMOCRACY.

00:08:11.954 --> 00:08:13.155
&gt;&gt; Bret: SEE YOU THINK THE

00:08:13.189 --> 00:08:13.706
PRESIDENT SHOULD OFFICIALLY

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:14.890
CONCEDE?

00:08:14.925 --> 00:08:17.614
&gt;&gt; Governor Hutchinson:

00:08:17.649 --> 00:08:20.331
WELL -- I UNDERSTAND THE LEGAL

00:08:20.332 --> 00:08:22.293
REASON WHY HE SHOULD NOT BECAUSE

00:08:22.294 --> 00:08:23.894
HE HAS APPEALS GOING, SO I

00:08:23.929 --> 00:08:26.600
RECOGNIZE THAT BUT BEYOND THAT,

00:08:26.634 --> 00:08:28.062
IT’S PRESIDENT-ELECT BIDEN.

00:08:28.096 --> 00:08:29.533
WE ARE WORKING WITH THE

00:08:29.534 --> 00:08:29.899
TRANSITION.

00:08:29.934 --> 00:08:31.776
THAT IS WHERE WE ARE.

00:08:31.777 --> 00:08:33.697
WE EXPECT THEM TO BE SWORN IN IN

00:08:33.731 --> 00:08:35.640
JANUARY EVEN THOUGH THERE’S

00:08:35.674 --> 00:08:37.256
GOING TO BE SOME CONTINUED

00:08:37.257 --> 00:08:38.247
REVIEWS, WHICH I RESPECT.

00:08:38.248 --> 00:08:40.245
AND IT’S NOT THAT IMPORTANT --

00:08:40.279 --> 00:08:41.864
THE TRANSITION IS WHAT IS

00:08:41.899 --> 00:08:42.122
IMPORTANT.

00:08:42.123 --> 00:08:44.692
THE WORDS OF PRESIDENT TRUMP ARE

00:08:44.694 --> 00:08:45.873
NOT QUITE AS SIGNIFICANT, BUT

00:08:45.875 --> 00:08:47.880
THE ACTIONS ARE IMPORTANT IN

00:08:47.914 --> 00:08:49.133
HELPING IN THIS TRANSITION TO

00:08:49.167 --> 00:08:52.212
MAKE SURE THAT PRESIDENT-ELECT

00:08:52.246 --> 00:08:52.637
BIDEN IS READY TO GO ON JANUARY

